"use strict";

/* THE TIMELINE - what actually happened, while the operator was busy.

   Split out of content.js when that module reached the size ceiling, because this is the
   dataset most likely to keep growing: every year adds events and none of the old ones stop
   being true.

   Each entry is a real, dated event with the source it came from, because the game claims to
   be a historical replay and a claim without a citation is just atmosphere. `imp` is not
   decoration either - an imp:3 event stops the clock, opens a dialog and awards a skill
   point, so raising one is a balance decision, not an editorial one. Most events are imp:2:
   worth reading in the feed, not worth interrupting for.

   Twelve of these carry an `fx` that reaches into the simulation - the venue failures, the
   supply-chain disclosures - and those are wired in applyEvent(). The rest are context, and
   context is the point: the operator should be able to see why the ground moved under them. */

const EVENTS=[
  {id:"conferenceprague11",date:"2011-11-25",title:"There are enough of us to book a room",dek:"An early European Bitcoin conference in Prague turns forum handles into a meeting programme.",body:"The organiser's announcement schedules the gathering for 25-27 November, with subjects spanning development, mining, law, economics and finance. Announced speakers include Amir Taaki and Rickard Falkvinge.<br><br>Bitcoin is becoming a community that can organise in person, rather than only a download and a discussion thread. That can make collaboration easier; it also creates stages, reputations and new opportunities to mistake confidence for expertise.",cat:"adoption",imp:2,storyPopup:true,conference:{visit:"Heard about it",scene:["A link appears in the forum: Prague, three days, actual people. You open it between checking the machine and wondering whether the electricity bill has become a hobby subscription.","For now, you stay home. The surprising part is not the travel. It is the programme: somebody expects enough miners, developers and merchants to spend a weekend arguing in the same building.","You bookmark the page. Until today, the community mostly lived behind usernames. Now it has a meeting place. Perhaps next time you will be in the room."]},src:"Organiser's original Bitcoin Forum announcement",url:"https://bitcointalk.org/index.php?topic=40272.0"},
  {id:"conferencesanjose13",date:"2013-05-17",title:"Your first conference: the future has a name badge",dek:"Bitcoin 2013 opens in San Jose, bringing mining, software, business and regulation into one conference.",body:"The Bitcoin Foundation organises The Future of Payments at the San Jose Convention Center, running 17-19 May. Its programme spans mining, technology, business and regulatory questions.<br><br>The useful change is practical: people building different parts of the system can meet, compare assumptions and find collaborators. A conference is a place to learn what exists and what still needs work. It cannot certify the projects selling themselves there.",cat:"adoption",imp:2,storyPopup:true,conference:{visit:"First visit · San Jose",scene:["This time you go. At registration, your name becomes something people can read without decoding a forum handle. You are briefly more interested in that than the badge lanyard deserves.","Between sessions, you drift into a conversation about mining. One person talks about the next machine, another about payments, and somebody asks how any of this fits the rules businesses already live under. Your little operation suddenly belongs to a much larger argument.","You leave with notes and possible contacts. The useful souvenir is a better question for every vendor: what works today, and what are you merely promising? The badge goes in a drawer. The questions come back to the mine."]},src:"Bitcoin Foundation conference announcement",url:"https://www.prlog.org/12051141-announcing-bitcoin-2013-the-future-of-payments.html"},
  {id:"conferencemiami21",date:"2021-06-05",title:"Miami: a country enters the conversation",dek:"Jack Mallers presents a recorded message from Nayib Bukele announcing plans for Bitcoin legal-tender legislation in El Salvador.",body:"At Bitcoin 2021 in Miami, Mallers introduces the announcement that President Bukele intends to submit a bill. This is a proposal on the conference stage, not yet an enacted law: the legislative vote follows on 9 June.<br><br>The question moves beyond whether people will buy bitcoin. It becomes how a national payment system, remittances, wallets and public policy might work around it. Access can widen while new dependencies appear around apps, conversion and state-backed infrastructure.",cat:"adoption",imp:2,storyPopup:true,conference:{visit:"Return visit · Miami",scene:["You come looking for tools and leave thinking about a country. On stage, Mallers introduces the recorded announcement. The scale of the conversation changes while you are still holding your conference notes.","In the imagined row beside you, somebody is already calling it the future. You write down a less glamorous question: how does a shopkeeper turn a payment into tomorrow's stock? A national announcement makes the opportunity bigger without answering every operational detail.","Back outside the session, the arguments continue. You are glad you came. You are also glad that your notes have a separate page for what was announced and what still has to happen."]},src:"Contemporaneous CoinDesk reporting",url:"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2021/06/05/president-of-el-salvador-says-hes-submitting-bill-to-make-bitcoin-legal-tender"},
  {id:"conferencenashville24",date:"2024-07-27",title:"Nashville: the politicians want the microphone",dek:"Donald Trump addresses Bitcoin 2024, while Senator Cynthia Lummis announces a strategic Bitcoin reserve proposal.",body:"At the Nashville conference, presidential candidate Trump proposes retaining government bitcoin as a strategic stockpile. Lummis separately announces a proposal for a reserve and a one-million-bitcoin purchase programme.<br><br>These are campaign commitments and a legislative proposal at this date, not completed purchases or an operating reserve. The stage shows how far Bitcoin has entered mainstream politics. It also makes the distinction between a speech, a bill and an implemented policy more important.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:2,storyPopup:true,conference:{visit:"Later visit · Nashville",scene:["You remember when the interesting development was enough people booking a room. Now the programme has a presidential candidate and a senator discussing reserves. The thing that ran beside your desk has become something politicians want to stand beside.","You listen, then split the notebook again: promised, proposed, implemented. The applause can put those categories together; your operating plan cannot.","On the way home, you have two competing impressions. Wider recognition could bring better access and investment. It could also tie the industry's mood to an election. Tomorrow the machines will still need power, and neither side of the conference argument will pay the bill for you."]},src:"Senator Lummis announcement; Trump speech transcript",url:"https://www.lummis.senate.gov/press-releases/lummis-announces-revolutionary-proposal-to-supercharge-the-dollar-bolster-u-s-economy/",sources:[{label:"Trump's conference speech transcript",url:"https://rollcall.com/factbase/trump/transcript/donald-trump-speech-bitcoin-conference-nashville-july-27-2024"}]},
  {id:"coremigration26",date:"2026-01-05",title:"The upgrade can lose the wallet",dek:"Bitcoin Core discloses a rare wallet-migration bug in versions 30.0 and 30.1 that can delete wallet-directory files.",body:"The affected path involves a failed migration of an old, unnamed wallet.dat file. Bitcoin Core withdraws the affected binaries and advises against wallet migration until a corrected release; users outside that migration path are unaffected.<br><br>The distinction matters: running a node, updating its software and converting a wallet are different operations. An official download can still contain a defect. Recovery preparation has to exist before the maintenance job that might make it necessary.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Core security advisory",url:"https://bitcoincore.org/en/2026/01/05/wallet-migration-bug/"},
  {id:"quantumresearch26",date:"2026-03-31",title:"The mathematics holds. The machines evolve.",dek:"Google publishes lower resource estimates for a future quantum attack on elliptic-curve cryptography.",body:"The research estimates what a sufficiently capable future quantum computer could need to solve the mathematical problem behind widely used digital signatures. It does not demonstrate a theft from Bitcoin or establish a date on which its keys will become breakable.<br><br>A signing key relies on more than keeping a file secret: it relies on an adversary being unable to recover that secret from public information. Hardware protection and offline storage address some threats; a change in computational capabilities raises another. Migration proposals, their review and their eventual adoption are separate stages.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Google Research",url:"https://research.google/blog/safeguarding-cryptocurrency-by-disclosing-quantum-vulnerabilities-responsibly/"},
  {id:"bip110closed",date:"2026-08-09",title:"You can change your rules. Can you bring the network?",dek:"BIP-110 is marked closed following a chain split with stalled mining, according to its official revision history.",body:"The proposal sought temporary consensus restrictions on arbitrary transaction data. Its supporters argued for keeping node costs down and Bitcoin focused on money; changing what blocks are valid made the dispute larger than a local choice about which transactions to relay.<br><br>The official proposal history records closure following a chain split with stalled mining. Publishing an implementation does not make other operators accept its rules. Independent verification gives each node a choice, but a usable shared ledger also needs participants to converge on a chain.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Improvement Proposal 110",url:"https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0110.mediawiki"},
  {id:"miningtoai26",date:"2026-09-01",title:"The power stays. The miners leave.",dek:"Hyperscale Data turns off Bitcoin miners at its Michigan facility to prepare the site for an AI customer.",body:"In an announcement published on 2 September, the company says all Bitcoin miners at this facility were switched off effective 1 September. The change prepares the site for an AI data-centre agreement; it does not mean Bitcoin mining has stopped everywhere the company operates.<br><br>A miner competes for more than block rewards. A power connection, a building and investment capital can serve another customer. Machines that still work can lose their place when the site has a more attractive use. The value of an ASIC and the value of the infrastructure around it can move in different directions.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Hyperscale Data company announcement",url:"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/hyperscale-data-has-ceased-bitcoin-mining-operations-in-michigan-as-it-fulfills-the-requirements-of-the-ai-data-center-master-services-agreement-expected-to-be-worth-approximately-1-2-billion-302867149.html"},
  {id:"genesis",date:"2009-01-03",title:"The Genesis Block",dek:"A monetary experiment begins with a newspaper headline embedded in block zero.",body:"No market exists - the game's own BTC/USD price stays dark until mid-2010 too - and hashing is tiny, the software is rough, and the network is an idea shared by a handful of people.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin whitepaper",url:"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},
  {id:"runningbitcoin",date:"2009-01-11",title:"\"Running bitcoin.\"",dek:"Cypherpunk Hal Finney posts the earliest public words about the software actually working.",body:"It is a small, technical remark from a well-known cryptography veteran - but it is the first public evidence that Bitcoin already had a second participant beyond its pseudonymous creator.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Hal_Finney"},
  {id:"firsttx",date:"2009-01-12",title:"The first transaction",dek:"Satoshi sends 10 BTC to Hal Finney in block 170 - the first payment between two people.",body:"The genesis block proved the software could run; this proves value could actually move between independent parties. Every later transaction on the network repeats this same small act.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Block_170"},
  {id:"firstprice",date:"2009-10-05",title:"A first price, of sorts",dek:"Someone finally puts a number on it: roughly 1,309 BTC per dollar, based on the electricity it cost to mine them.",body:"It is less a market than an educated guess - there is barely a buyer or seller in sight - but it is the first attempt to price the network in a currency everyone already understood.",cat:"markets",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"bitcointalk",date:"2009-11-22",title:"A forum for the forming community",dek:"Development chatter and mining tips move to a dedicated message board.",body:"For years this is where protocol changes, exchange rates and hardware advice get argued out in public - a rare direct line into a still-tiny, mostly anonymous community.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"BitcoinTalk",url:"https://bitcointalk.org/"},
  {id:"subreddit",date:"2010-09-09",title:"r/Bitcoin opens its doors",dek:"A subreddit gives the community a faster, louder gathering point than the forum.",body:"Price chatter, technical debate and no shortage of the network's earliest running jokes find a home here - a sign Bitcoin's audience is starting to outgrow one technical forum.",cat:"adoption",imp:1,src:"Reddit",url:"https://www.reddit.com/r/Bitcoin/"},
  {id:"satoshigone",date:"2010-12-12",title:"Satoshi's last known message",dek:"Bitcoin's pseudonymous creator mentions moving on to other things, then goes quiet.",body:"No protocol change marks the moment; the software keeps running exactly as designed. It becomes the clearest proof yet that Bitcoin does not depend on any one person staying in charge of it.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Satoshi_Nakamoto"},
  {id:"wiredprofile",date:"2011-11-23",title:"A national magazine takes notice",dek:"Wired runs a long profile chasing Bitcoin's mystery, its money and the hunt for Satoshi.",body:"Coverage like this carries Bitcoin out of forums and mailing lists and into a mainstream audience that had never heard of it - for better and worse, once Silk Road becomes part of the same story.",cat:"adoption",imp:2,src:"Wired",url:"https://www.wired.com/"},
  {id:"overflow",date:"2010-08-15",title:"The value-overflow bug is contained",dek:"An invalid transaction creates an impossible quantity of bitcoin; the network rolls back through an emergency upgrade.",body:"The episode is an early lesson in the value of many people independently running and reviewing software. Consensus is resilient, but implementation bugs still matter.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Value_overflow_incident"},
  {id:"pizza",date:"2010-05-22",title:"Two pizzas, 10,000 BTC",dek:"Bitcoin crosses from abstract units into a memorable real-world exchange.",body:"The purchase becomes a cultural price-discovery milestone. Liquidity remains almost nonexistent.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Laszlo_Hanyecz"},
  {id:"mtgoxopen",celebrate:true,date:"2010-07-17",title:"Continuous trading arrives",dek:"Mt. Gox becomes the dominant early venue and gives Bitcoin a visible dollar price - and its balance sheet, not yours, now holds the keys to whatever you deposit.",body:"The convenience is transformative, and so is the concentration of counterparty risk: in this game, anything left on a venue counts as custodial BTC, not self-held bitcoin, until you withdraw it to a wallet you control.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/"},
  {id:"parity",date:"2011-02-09",title:"Bitcoin reaches dollar parity",dek:"For the first time, one bitcoin trades around one U.S. dollar.",body:"The number is small, but it makes the experiment legible to a much wider audience and gives miners a clearer economic signal.",cat:"markets",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"silk",date:"2011-02-01",title:"Censorship resistance meets the dark web",dek:"Silk Road creates demand and draws intense scrutiny.",body:"Bitcoin becomes entangled with a geopolitical argument about borders, surveillance and illicit finance that will follow it for years.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/ross-ulbricht-creator-and-owner-silk-road-website-found-guilty-manhattan-federal-court"},
  {id:"wikileaksdonate",date:"2011-06-14",title:"WikiLeaks turns to Bitcoin donations",dek:"A publisher cut off from conventional payment rails accepts Bitcoin support.",body:"The episode becomes an early proof that Bitcoin can move value when conventional intermediaries refuse service.",cat:"civil society",imp:2,src:"WikiLeaks",url:"https://wikileaks.org/donate.html"},
  {id:"halving1",date:"2012-11-28",title:"The first halving",dek:"New supply per block falls from 50 BTC to 25 BTC.",body:"The schedule works exactly as coded. In the game's own payout formula, expected BTC/day is blocks × (subsidy + fees) - halving the subsidy overnight cuts miner revenue immediately, and inefficient hardware feels it first.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"foundation",date:"2012-09-27",title:"The Bitcoin Foundation forms",dek:"Early industry participants create an advocacy and standards-oriented organisation.",body:"It reflects Bitcoin's growing public profile and the recurring tension between informal open-source coordination and representative institutions.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin Foundation archive",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Bitcoin_Foundation"},
  {id:"fincen",date:"2013-03-18",title:"Washington defines the perimeter",dek:"FinCEN issues guidance for virtual-currency businesses.",body:"Bitcoin is no longer too small for formal financial regulation. Compliance becomes part of the infrastructure.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"FinCEN",url:"https://www.fincen.gov/resources/statutes-regulations/guidance/application-fincens-regulations-persons-administering"},
  {id:"cyprus",date:"2013-03-25",title:"Cyprus and the bank bail-in",dek:"Capital controls and losses for uninsured depositors sharpen the case for assets outside banks.",body:"Bitcoin rallies during the crisis, but the exact causal contribution remains debated - the same distinction every event card in this game draws: a price move shown as context, never as proof. The event becomes part of Bitcoin's political mythology regardless.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"European Commission",url:"https://economy-finance.ec.europa.eu/eu-financial-assistance/euro-area-countries/financial-assistance-cyprus_en"},
  {id:"silkseized",date:"2013-10-02",title:"The Silk Road is seized",dek:"U.S. authorities shut the marketplace and seize a vast hoard of bitcoin.",body:"The network continues. The state demonstrates that Bitcoin is censorship-resistant infrastructure, not immunity from law enforcement.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/manhattan-us-attorney-announces-seizure-additional-28-million-worth-bitcoins-belonging"},
  {id:"china13",date:"2013-12-05",title:"China restricts financial institutions",dek:"The People's Bank of China warns institutions away from Bitcoin business.",body:"Policy risk in the world's most important mining and trading region becomes a recurring market force.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/english/130721/2013/index.html"},
  {id:"mtgox",date:"2014-02-24",title:"Mt. Gox goes dark",dek:"The largest early exchange suspends trading and enters bankruptcy.",body:"Bitcoin does not live on an exchange; an exchange holds keys on a customer's behalf. The game scores only self-held hot and cold BTC - anyone who left their balance on Mt. Gox learned that distinction the hardest way possible.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/",fx:"mtgox"},
  {id:"auction",date:"2014-06-27",title:"The U.S. auctions seized bitcoin",dek:"A government sale turns confiscated coins into an institutional asset lot.",body:"States may prosecute Bitcoin-enabled crime while treating the asset itself as saleable property.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/acting-manhattan-us-attorney-announces-forfeiture-48-million-sale-silk-road-bitcoins"},
  {id:"bitlicense",date:"2015-06-03",title:"New York's BitLicense",dek:"A major financial centre creates a dedicated licensing regime.",body:"Consumer protection and compliance arrive with consolidation: smaller operators face costs they cannot absorb.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"New York DFS",url:"https://www.dfs.ny.gov/virtual_currency_businesses"},
  {id:"halving2",date:"2016-07-09",title:"The second halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 12.5 BTC.",body:"Mining economics tighten again: the same subsidy term in your expected-BTC/day formula is cut in half, rewarding scale and efficient silicon over brute machine count.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"bitfinexhack",date:"2016-08-02",title:"Bitfinex is hacked",dek:"A major exchange loses roughly 120,000 BTC and socialises losses across customer balances.",body:"The venue continues operating, but custody convenience comes with a reminder: exchange balances are claims exposed to the operator's security model, and in this game they sit in custodial BTC, not the self-held total that counts toward your final score.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Bitfinex security incident",url:"https://www.bitfinex.com/posts/213",fx:"bitfinex"},
  {id:"winklevossetfdenied",date:"2017-03-10",title:"The first Winklevoss ETF bid is denied",dek:"The SEC rejects the proposed rule change that would have listed the Winklevoss Bitcoin Trust.",body:"First proposed in 2013, the trust is rejected four years later: regulators say the exchange hasn't shown adequate protection against fraud and manipulation in the underlying bitcoin market. Wall Street access will have to wait.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/rules/sro/batsbzx/2017/34-80206.pdf"},
  {id:"japan",date:"2017-04-01",title:"Japan recognises Bitcoin payments",dek:"A national framework pulls exchanges into regulation.",body:"Recognition broadens access while making custody businesses more legible to the state.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"Japan Financial Services Agency",url:"https://www.fsa.go.jp/en/policy/virtual_currency/index.html"},
  {id:"segwit",date:"2017-08-24",title:"SegWit activates",dek:"A major soft fork changes how transaction data is structured and expands effective block capacity.",body:"The upgrade improves transaction malleability handling and opens a path for second-layer designs. It is also a landmark in Bitcoin's decentralised governance story.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Optech",url:"https://bitcoinops.org/en/topics/segwit/"},
  {id:"china17",date:"2017-09-04",title:"China closes the trading door",dek:"Authorities move against ICOs and domestic crypto exchanges.",body:"Trading migrates offshore. Mining remains concentrated in China, leaving the network - and any in-game facility still sitting in an exposed region - vulnerable to the policy break that follows four years later.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/english/130721/3131759/index.html"},
  {id:"futures",date:"2017-12-17",title:"Bitcoin futures reach CME",dek:"A systemically important derivatives venue launches regulated futures.",body:"Institutional access expands, including the ability to express a short view.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"CME Group",url:"https://www.cmegroup.com/media-room/press-releases/2017/12/17/cme_group_self-certifiesbitcoinfuturestolaunchdec18.html"},
  {id:"lightningmainnet",date:"2018-03-15",title:"Lightning reaches mainnet beta",dek:"A payment network built on Bitcoin begins its cautious public rollout.",body:"Lightning promises faster, lower-value payments without putting every transfer directly on-chain. In the game it arrives from 2018 as routing liquidity - lock hot-wallet BTC into channels to earn a small daily fee, with an online archival or relay node required to keep it running.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Lightning Labs",url:"https://lightning.engineering/posts/2018-03-15-lightning-mainnet-beta"},
  {id:"whitepaper10",date:"2018-10-31",title:"Ten years of the whitepaper",dek:"Bitcoin's founding paper reaches a decade in circulation.",body:"The system has moved from an obscure proposal to a global market, while its original questions about money, trust and self-custody remain active.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Bitcoin whitepaper",url:"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},
  {id:"quadriga",date:"2019-02-05",title:"QuadrigaCX collapses",dek:"Canada's largest exchange is unable to return customer assets after the death of its founder and a severe custody shortfall.",body:"Users learn again that a balance on an exchange is not the same thing as bitcoin controlled by your own keys - exactly the line this game draws between self-held hot and cold wallets and everything else.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"Ontario Securities Commission",url:"https://www.osc.ca/en/news-events/news/osc-concludes-investigation-quadrigacx-and-its-founder-gerald-cotten",fx:"quadriga"},
  {id:"covid",date:"2020-03-12",title:"The global dash for cash",dek:"As COVID-19 shocks markets, Bitcoin falls with nearly every liquid risk asset.",body:"The crisis punctures the idea that Bitcoin is always an immediate safe haven, and the same shock ripples into the game's spare-parts market: lead times stretch to 42 days and prices jump 2.25× until mid-2021, so a fleet already due for service gets harder to keep running.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"World Health Organization",url:"https://www.who.int/europe/emergencies/situations/covid-19"},
  {id:"halving3",date:"2020-05-11",title:"The third halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 6.25 BTC amid extraordinary monetary expansion.",body:"The contrast between fixed issuance and discretionary policy becomes Bitcoin's dominant macro story - and in-game, every miner's expected daily BTC drops with the subsidy, regardless of how much fiat was spent on hardware.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"paypal",date:"2020-10-21",title:"PayPal brings Bitcoin to its users",dek:"A global payments company launches buying, holding and selling of cryptocurrency for eligible customers.",body:"Access broadens dramatically, even as the custodial model reminds users that an account balance is different from keys and direct settlement.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"PayPal",url:"https://newsroom.paypal-corp.com/2020-10-21-PayPal-Launches-a-New-Service-Enabling-Users-to-Buy-Hold-and-Sell-Cryptocurrency"},
  {id:"tesla",date:"2021-02-08",title:"Bitcoin enters a corporate treasury",dek:"Tesla discloses a $1.5 billion purchase and plans to accept bitcoin.",body:"A public company turns a fringe treasury strategy into a boardroom question worldwide - the same corporate Bitcoin-treasury bet that Strategy's fiat-priced securities in this game's Treasury exist to proxy.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. SEC filing",url:"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000156459021004599/tsla-10k_20201231.htm"},
  {id:"elsalvador",date:"2021-06-09",title:"El Salvador makes Bitcoin legal tender",dek:"A sovereign state puts Bitcoin into national law.",body:"The experiment expands Bitcoin's geopolitical role and triggers debate over adoption, coercion, remittances and sovereign risk.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"El Salvador Legislative Assembly",url:"https://www.asamblea.gob.sv/node/11282"},
  {id:"chinaexit",date:"2021-06-21",title:"China expels the miners",dek:"Provincial shutdowns drive the largest geographic migration in proof-of-work history.",body:"Network hash rate collapses, then recovers elsewhere. Cheap power is worthless when political permission disappears - the same relocation risk the game models whenever a facility moves into or out of an exposed region.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"People's Bank of China",url:"https://www.pbc.gov.cn/en/3688253/3689012/4353814/index.html",fx:"china"},
  {id:"riottexas",date:"2021-08-01",title:"A Texas miner grows grid-sized",dek:"Riot Platforms' build-out at its Rockdale facility becomes large enough to be a genuine factor in ERCOT's regional power balance.",body:"Texas courted Bitcoin miners as flexible, curtailable load; Riot's own scale-up is one of the clearest examples of that bet paying off for the grid operator during tight periods - and a reminder that any facility sharing that grid, yours included, will feel the same regional price pressure when demand spikes.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"ERCOT",url:"https://www.ercot.com/",fx:"riotx"},
  {id:"taproot",date:"2021-11-14",title:"Taproot activates",dek:"A privacy- and efficiency-oriented soft fork reaches the network after a broad signalling process.",body:"The upgrade expands the design space for complex spending conditions while making many of them look more like ordinary transactions on-chain.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Optech",url:"https://bitcoinops.org/en/topics/taproot/"},
  {id:"kazakh",date:"2022-01-05",title:"Kazakhstan goes dark",dek:"Unrest and a nationwide internet shutdown hit a major post-China mining hub.",body:"Geographic diversification helped the network, but miners who chased one cheap grid discovered a new concentration risk - the same connectivity-outage exposure the game prices into every region's jurisdiction risk.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:2,src:"Internet Society",url:"https://pulse.internetsociety.org/shutdowns/internet-shutdown-in-kazakhstan",fx:"kazakh"},
  {id:"ukraine",date:"2022-02-24",title:"War tests borderless money",dek:"Russia invades Ukraine; sanctions, donations and capital controls put crypto rails under scrutiny.",body:"Bitcoin is used by donors and individuals while governments focus on sanctions enforcement. The same neutrality serves conflicting human purposes.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"European Council",url:"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/policies/eu-response-ukraine-invasion/"},
  {id:"ukrdonate",date:"2022-02-26",title:"Ukraine opens crypto donation channels",dek:"Public crypto addresses become part of a rapid global fundraising effort.",body:"The moment shows both the speed and transparency trade-offs of borderless donations during a humanitarian and military emergency.",cat:"civil society",imp:2,src:"Ukraine digital aid",url:"https://donate.thedigital.gov.ua/"},
  {id:"useo",date:"2022-03-09",title:"A whole-of-government U.S. strategy",dek:"The White House orders agencies to coordinate digital-asset policy.",body:"Bitcoin is now a matter of consumer protection, competitiveness, illicit finance, energy and national security at once.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"White House archive",url:"https://bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2022/03/09/executive-order-on-ensuring-responsible-development-of-digital-assets/"},
  {id:"terra",date:"2022-05-12",title:"Leverage unwinds",dek:"The Terra ecosystem collapses and forced selling spreads through crypto markets.",body:"Bitcoin keeps producing blocks, but the credit system built around digital assets proves deeply connected and fragile.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"Federal Reserve",url:"https://www.federalreserve.gov/publications/november-2022-financial-stability-report-digital-assets.htm"},
  {id:"celsius",date:"2022-06-12",title:"A crypto lender freezes withdrawals",dek:"Celsius Network halts withdrawals, swaps and transfers, citing extreme market conditions.",body:"Customers who had lent coins, or pledged them against loans, found them frozen, and the lender filed for bankruptcy a month later. A loan against your bitcoin is only as safe as whoever holds the collateral: a lender that held one key of a multisig could not move the coins, and one that held all of them could.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Wikipedia: Celsius Network",url:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celsius_Network",fx:"lenders"},
  {id:"voyager",date:"2022-07-01",title:"Another crypto lender stops withdrawals",dek:"Voyager Digital suspends trading, deposits and withdrawals, and files for bankruptcy days later.",body:"It had lent heavily to a hedge fund that could not repay. Customers who pledged coins against loans, or left them to earn interest, became creditors. The same lesson as a fortnight earlier, from a different company that looked the same from outside.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Wikipedia: Voyager Digital",url:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyager_Digital",fx:"lender:voyager"},
  {id:"blockfi",date:"2022-11-10",title:"A third lender halts withdrawals",dek:"BlockFi pauses withdrawals after the collapse of FTX, to which it was heavily exposed, and files for bankruptcy within weeks.",body:"Unlike the first two, its customers eventually recovered most of what they were owed. Exposure to one failing counterparty was enough to stop a lender that had survived the summer.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Wikipedia: BlockFi",url:"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BlockFi",fx:"lender:blockfi"},
  {id:"merge",date:"2022-09-15",title:"Ethereum leaves proof-of-work",dek:"Ethereum completes its transition to proof-of-stake, making Bitcoin's proof-of-work model stand out more sharply.",body:"The contrast reframes energy debates: Bitcoin miners face more scrutiny, but also a clearer opportunity to demonstrate flexible demand and grid services.",cat:"network",imp:1,src:"Ethereum Foundation",url:"https://ethereum.org/en/roadmap/merge/"},
  {id:"computenorthbankrupt",date:"2022-09-22",title:"Compute North files for bankruptcy",dek:"A major U.S. mining host collapses under its own expansion debt, pushing a wave of hosted ASICs onto the resale market.",body:"Compute North grew fast on borrowed money and cheap power deals; when both tightened at once, Chapter 11 followed. Displaced hosting clients and secured creditors alike start moving hardware, and the in-game secondary ASIC market gets measurably cheaper for a few months.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Bankruptcy Court, Southern District of Texas",url:"https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/bitcoin-miner-compute-north-files-bankruptcy-2022-09-22/",fx:"computenorthx"},
  {id:"coldcardentropy",date:"2026-07-30",title:"Coldcard seeds are being drained",dek:"A five-year-old firmware defect made some hardware-wallet seeds guessable. The thefts began within the hour.",body:"Coinkite has disclosed that a configuration error introduced with a March 2021 firmware migration caused some COLDCARD devices to fall back on a software random number generator instead of the hardware entropy source when generating a seed. Reported analysis puts the resulting key strength as low as 40 bits rather than 128 - weak enough to search.<br><br>Thefts began on 30 July 2026. Galaxy Research's running tally reached roughly 1,816 BTC, about $116M, taken from more than 5,200 addresses across four waves; the first wave moved around 594 BTC in twenty-five minutes. Coinkite says it is preparing a post-mortem rather than estimating customer losses.<br><br>The remedy is not a firmware update. In Coinkite's own words, updating \u201ccorrects future seed generation but does not repair an existing affected seed\u201d. A seed generated in that window is weak on any device you move it to, forever. The only fix is a new seed and a migration.<br><br>What did hold: a wallet requiring two independently generated keys does not open because one of them was guessable.",cat:"custody",imp:3,fx:"coldcardentropy",
    src:"Coinkite security disclosure history; Galaxy Research tallies via TRM Labs",
    url:"https://coinkite.com/historical-disclosures"},
  {id:"ledgerbreach",date:"2020-07-29",title:"Ledger discloses a customer-data breach",dek:"A hardware-wallet vendor's e-commerce and marketing database was accessed. Devices and funds are not affected; customer records are.",body:"Ledger has announced that an unauthorised third party accessed its e-commerce and marketing database, exposing contact details for around a million subscribers and order information for a smaller group of customers. The company states that no payment details and no device secrets were involved, and that the security of the devices themselves is unchanged.<br><br>That distinction is real and it is also cold comfort. A list of people known to have bought a hardware wallet, with their delivery addresses attached, is a target list. What follows is phishing, convincing fakes of vendor emails, and in some cases threats made in person. Nothing about the leak lets anyone spend your coins; everything about it helps them try to persuade you to.<br><br>A different device does not undo this. The record of the purchase already left.",cat:"custody",imp:2,fx:"ledgerleak",
    src:"Ledger, \u201cAddressing the July 2020 e-commerce and marketing data breach\u201d",
    url:"https://www.ledger.com/addressing-the-july-2020-e-commerce-and-marketing-data-breach"},
  {id:"ftx",date:"2022-11-11",title:"FTX files for bankruptcy",dek:"A globally prominent exchange fails with an enormous customer shortfall.",body:"Proof of reserves, segregation and self-custody return to the centre of the debate. Reputation is not the same thing as solvency - and a balance you haven't withdrawn is a claim on the venue's solvency, not bitcoin you hold.",cat:"custody",imp:3,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/samuel-bankman-fried-sentenced-25-years-his-orchestration-multiple-fraudulent-schemes",fx:"ftx"},
  {id:"corescientificbankrupt",date:"2022-12-21",title:"Core Scientific files for Chapter 11",dek:"One of the largest publicly traded Bitcoin miners in the U.S. seeks bankruptcy protection.",body:"A punishing mix of falling BTC prices, a strong dollar and heavy equipment debt catches up with one of the sector's biggest names. The resulting liquidation adds even more secondhand ASICs to a market already softened by Compute North's collapse months earlier.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=CORZ",fx:"corescix"},
  {id:"banks",date:"2023-03-10",title:"A banking crisis hits crypto's rails",dek:"Silicon Valley Bank fails after Silvergate winds down; access to dollars tightens.",body:"Bitcoin rallies as bank fragility revives its origin story, even while crypto firms lose critical banking infrastructure.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"Federal Reserve review",url:"https://www.federalreserve.gov/publications/review-of-the-federal-reserves-supervision-and-regulation-of-silicon-valley-bank.htm"},
  {id:"ordinals",date:"2023-01-21",title:"Inscriptions reshape the fee market",dek:"Ordinal inscriptions bring new kinds of data and demand to Bitcoin block space.",body:"The debate is immediate: permissionless block space can invite unexpected uses, and miners gain another reminder that transaction fees - the second term in every block's payout, alongside the subsidy - may matter more over time.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Ordinals",url:"https://ordinals.com/"},
  {id:"mica",date:"2023-05-16",title:"Europe adopts MiCA",dek:"The EU creates a bloc-wide framework for crypto-asset services.",body:"Regulatory clarity can increase compliance cost and institutional confidence at the same time.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"Council of the EU",url:"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2023/05/16/digital-finance-council-adopts-new-rules-on-markets-in-crypto-assets-mica/"},
  {id:"binance",date:"2023-11-21",title:"Binance settles U.S. criminal charges",dek:"The world's largest crypto exchange agrees to major penalties and compliance commitments.",body:"The case reinforces a durable lesson for the player: liquidity venues are businesses with legal, operational and counterparty risk - not neutral extensions of the protocol, and not the self-held BTC the game scores at the end of a run.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"U.S. Department of Justice",url:"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/binance-and-its-ceo-plead-guilty-federal-charges"},
  {id:"etf",date:"2024-01-10",title:"U.S. spot Bitcoin products approved",dek:"The SEC approves exchange rules for spot Bitcoin ETPs.",body:"Brokerage accounts gain price exposure at scale. An ETF is not self-custodied bitcoin and cannot validate or transact on the network - in the game's own header it sits in illiquid fiat, not the self-held BTC that counts toward your score.",cat:"markets",imp:3,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/gensler-statement-spot-bitcoin-011023",fx:"etf"},
  {id:"halving4",date:"2024-04-20",title:"The fourth halving",dek:"The subsidy falls to 3.125 BTC as fee-market experiments intensify.",body:"Every miner now competes for half the new issuance available a day earlier - check your mining-share economics now, since the subsidy component of your payout has just halved again.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin developer reference",url:"https://developer.bitcoin.org/reference/block_chain.html"},
  {id:"mtgoxrepay",date:"2024-07-05",title:"Mt. Gox repayments begin",dek:"After a decade of insolvency proceedings, distributions to former customers finally start.",body:"The long aftermath is a sobering capstone to the early-exchange era: custody failures can outlast multiple market cycles - a reminder that the safest time to withdraw a venue balance was always before the failure, not after.",cat:"custody",imp:1,src:"Mt. Gox rehabilitation",url:"https://www.mtgox.com/"},
  {id:"policy25",date:"2025-01-23",title:"Washington changes direction",dek:"A new executive order promotes U.S. leadership in digital assets and revokes the 2022 order.",body:"The regulatory pendulum becomes a market variable in its own right.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/strengthening-american-leadership-in-digital-financial-technology/"},
  {id:"realbedford",date:"2025-02-20",title:"The Winklevoss twins buy into Real Bedford",dek:"Winklevoss Capital finalises a $4.5 million investment for a 45% stake in the non-league football club.",body:"Eight years after their Bitcoin ETF was rejected, Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss become co-owners of Peter McCormack's Real Bedford FC. Bitcoin's institutional era now includes a very literal attempt to climb the English football pyramid.",cat:"adoption",imp:1,src:"Sky Sports and Companies House",url:"https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/13312885/real-bedford-fc-cryptocurrency-investors-cameron-and-tyler-winklevoss-inject-gbp3-58m-and-become-part-owners"},
  {id:"reserve",date:"2025-03-06",title:"The United States establishes a Bitcoin reserve",dek:"An executive order directs forfeited government BTC into a Strategic Bitcoin Reserve.",body:"The asset once seized mainly as criminal proceeds is recast as a strategic state holding. Sovereign game theory is no longer hypothetical.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/establishment-of-the-strategic-bitcoin-reserve-and-united-states-digital-asset-stockpile/"},
  {id:"inkind",date:"2025-07-29",title:"Crypto ETPs gain in-kind mechanics",dek:"The SEC permits in-kind creations and redemptions for crypto exchange-traded products.",body:"Market plumbing becomes more efficient, but retail ETF holders still own shares rather than spendable bitcoin.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission",url:"https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/uyeda-statement-crypto-exchange-traded-products-072925"},
  {id:"framework26",date:"2026-05-18",title:"Digital assets enter the regulatory framework",dek:"The U.S. pushes digital-asset market structure deeper into mainstream financial policy.",body:"Bitcoin's story has travelled from a mailing list to state balance sheets and national regulatory architecture. The protocol still settles blocks on its own clock.",cat:"geopolitics",imp:3,src:"The White House",url:"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/2026/05/fact-sheet-president-donald-j-trump-integrates-financial-technology-innovation-into-regulatory-frameworks/"},
  {id:"gox2011",date:"2011-06-19",title:"Mt. Gox prints one cent",dek:"A stolen credential floods the book and the largest exchange trades bitcoin at a penny.",body:"Nothing was wrong with the network - blocks kept arriving on schedule - and that is the lesson. An exchange is a company with a database, and its price is its own opinion until you have withdrawn. Coins you cannot move are coins somebody else is holding for you.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Mt._Gox"},
  {id:"linode",date:"2012-03-01",title:"A hosting company loses other people's coins",dek:"Intruders reach Linode's management console and empty the hot wallets of everything running on it.",body:"Roughly 46,000 BTC left in an afternoon, a mining pool's operating float among them. Every wallet involved was hot because hot was convenient, and convenience is exactly what an attacker inherits. The coins were not really stolen from their owners; they were stolen from the machine their owners trusted.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"avalon",date:"2013-01-19",title:"The first ASICs ship",dek:"Purpose-built silicon reaches customers, and every general-purpose miner is obsolete at once.",body:"A CPU could mine in 2009 because nothing better existed. GPUs ended that, FPGAs squeezed it further, and an ASIC ends the argument permanently: a chip that can do nothing except this, thousands of times more efficiently than anything that can also do something else. From here, competing means buying the current generation - and the current generation has a shelf life.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Mining_hardware_comparison"},
  {id:"crash2013",date:"2013-04-10",title:"$266, and an exchange that could not keep up",dek:"The price triples in a fortnight, then halves in a day while the main venue stalls under load.",body:"The order book was not the problem; the plumbing was. Trading halted, withdrawals queued, and holders found that a quoted price is worth only what the venue can actually settle. For an operation funding its power bill from sales, the number on screen and the money in the account are different things.",cat:"markets",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"irsproperty",date:"2014-03-25",title:"The IRS calls it property",dek:"Notice 2014-21 settles the American tax treatment: not currency but property - and mined coins are income the day they arrive.",body:"For a miner that second half is the sharper one. Coins are taxable at their value on the day the block lands, sold or not, and that same day sets the cost basis for disposing of them later. An operation that mines through a rising year and sells nothing can still owe tax in cash it never received.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"U.S. Internal Revenue Service",url:"https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-drop/n-14-21.pdf"},
  {id:"msaccepts",date:"2014-12-11",title:"Microsoft takes bitcoin",dek:"One of the largest software companies begins accepting BTC for digital goods in its stores.",body:"Not a payment revolution - balances were converted to dollars immediately and the amounts were small - but a large, cautious company deciding the reputational risk had fallen far enough to be worth a press release.",cat:"adoption",imp:1,src:"Microsoft",url:"https://www.microsoft.com/"},
  {id:"bitstamphack",date:"2015-01-04",title:"Bitstamp loses its hot wallet",dek:"A European exchange is drained of roughly 19,000 BTC and suspends service to rebuild.",body:"Bitstamp survived it, paid customers from its own reserves and reopened - which makes it the useful counterexample to Gox. The difference was not luck but a smaller hot balance and a company able to absorb the loss. Both of those are decisions, taken long before the breach.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Bitstamp",url:"https://www.bitstamp.net/"},
  {id:"blocksizewar",date:"2015-08-15",title:"The block-size war begins",dek:"A rival implementation ships with bigger blocks, and the question of who decides the rules becomes public.",body:"It ran for two years and was never really about megabytes. If miners, exchanges, developers or users can each change the rules, the rules are whatever the strongest faction wants, and the one property worth having is gone. The eventual answer was that none of them could change them alone - which is why nothing changed quickly.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/Block_size_limit_controversy"},
  {id:"daofork",date:"2016-07-20",title:"Ethereum rewrites its own ledger",dek:"After a contract is drained, Ethereum hard-forks to reverse the theft; the unreversed chain survives as Ethereum Classic.",body:"A ledger that can be edited when the loss is large enough is a ledger with an editor. Reasonable people took both sides, and the split is the clearest experiment anyone has run on what immutability is actually worth. Bitcoin has never reversed a theft, including every one on this page.",cat:"network",imp:2,src:"Ethereum Foundation",url:"https://ethereum.org/"},
  {id:"coincheck",date:"2018-01-26",title:"Coincheck loses half a billion dollars",dek:"A Japanese exchange is drained of assets held in a hot wallet with no multisignature protection.",body:"The post-mortem found the balance had been left hot for operational convenience, by a company short of the staff to do it properly. Custody failures are rarely exotic cryptography. They are ordinary decisions about where the coins sit while everybody is busy.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Japan Financial Services Agency",url:"https://www.fsa.go.jp/en/"},
  {id:"hashwar",date:"2018-11-15",title:"The hash war",dek:"Two camps point rented hash rate at each other's chain, and mining becomes an instrument of a governance dispute.",body:"For weeks, hash rate was spent not on securing a ledger but on out-mining an opponent, on both chains, at a loss to everyone doing it. It is the plainest demonstration of what proof of work buys: security is rented, priced in electricity, and points wherever it is paid to point. Every operator's machines are part of that answer whether they think about it or not.",cat:"network",imp:3,src:"Bitcoin Wiki",url:"https://en.bitcoin.it/wiki/History"},
  {id:"binancehack",date:"2019-05-07",title:"Binance loses 7,000 BTC",dek:"The largest exchange by volume is drained of a hot wallet and covers the loss from its own insurance fund.",body:"The company briefly floated asking miners to reorganise the chain to undo it, then dropped the idea within a day. That it was raised at all, by the largest venue in the market, is the part worth keeping: the ledger holds because rewriting it is expensive and unpopular, not because it is impossible.",cat:"custody",imp:2,src:"Binance",url:"https://www.binance.com/"},
  {id:"libra",date:"2019-06-18",title:"Facebook proposes a currency",dek:"A social network with billions of users announces a global stablecoin, and regulators answer within days.",body:"It never launched. What it did was force finance ministries to take public positions on private money years earlier than they intended, and much of the regulatory architecture that followed - for stablecoins and for everything adjacent - was drafted in the alarm it caused.",cat:"policy",imp:2,src:"Reuters",url:"https://www.reuters.com/"},
  {id:"bakkt",date:"2019-09-23",title:"Futures that settle in coins",dek:"An exchange operator owned by the NYSE's parent launches physically settled Bitcoin futures.",body:"Cash-settled futures let institutions trade the price without ever touching the asset. Physical settlement means somebody has to deliver actual bitcoin, which requires regulated custody - and that plumbing is what the later spot products were built on.",cat:"markets",imp:1,src:"Intercontinental Exchange",url:"https://www.ice.com/"},
];
